course: dictionary
lesson: 15811
title: Unchecked
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To check means to look at something carefully to see if it is right, safe or under control. Unchecked is the same word with un- at the front, which often means not. So unchecked means not checked, not controlled, or not looked over.
explain: «The fire spread unchecked across the dry hillside.» Nothing stopped it, so it kept growing. «Her homework was unchecked, so the three spelling mistakes were never found.» Nobody had looked it over. The words around unchecked tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. On a computer, «The box next to Email is unchecked» means the box has no tick, so that option is off. One word, three meanings: the context tells you which one to use.
fact: Unchecked means not controlled or stopped, so it can grow or spread.
fact: Unchecked can also mean not looked over or tested, like «unchecked homework».
fact: An unchecked box has no tick in it, so the option is off.
fact: Useful phrases are go unchecked, left unchecked and spread unchecked.
fact: The prefix un- at the start of a word often means not, as in unchecked, unsafe and unkind.
exercise: «The fire spread unchecked across the hillside.» What does unchecked mean here? | Checked and approved by the teacher | *Not controlled or stopped | Carefully put away | Painted bright red
exercise: «Her unchecked homework had three spelling mistakes.» What does unchecked mean here? | Written in pen | *Not looked over or tested | Very long | Finished early
exercise: On the computer, the box next to Email is unchecked. What does that tell you? | The box is full of colour | The box is broken | *The option is off | The option is on
test: «Germs left unchecked can make people very ill.» What does unchecked mean here? | Washed away with soap | *Not stopped or controlled | Turned into a game | Hidden in a drawer
test: «The rumour went around the school ____.» Which word fills the gap best? | *unchecked | unlucky | unkind | untidy
exam: «The teacher found three mistakes in my unchecked work.» What does unchecked mean here? | Brightly coloured | Found under the bed | Given a prize | *Not looked over
